WEBVTT

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.080
Shuurei and Seiran were seeking the source of the counterfeit money and artworks.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.250
Walking with them was Shin Shou, also known as Tan-tan,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.530
who had proposed unenthusiastically to Shuurei.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:47.460
At the same time, Ryuuki and the others were trying to find Karin,

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.210
a woman who might know the whereabouts of Heki Yukoku.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.840
Thank you.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.280
I wonder who this Karin-san is.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.420
Me too.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.880
We've had it easy,

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.020
because she's given her expert opinion at all the stores and galleries we've visited.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.900
Who would've thought we'd be able to collect so many forgeries?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.430
I thought we'd be lucky to get a tip about the art dealer who's been buying the originals.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.350
Who is that?

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:28.290
The way he carries himself... He's not an amateur.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.920
What's wrong?

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.190
Well...

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.100
Ah, it's nothing.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.420
So, where are you gonna drag me next?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.680
Let's see...

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.630
Why?

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:58.530
Why on Earth is she so obsessed with housewares stores, wholesale dealers, and salt merchants?

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.090
Tan-tan-kun, don't you get it?

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.030
Not in the slightest.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.330
Then think about it.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.600
If you don't use your head, you'll become even more of an idiot.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:14.390
Okay, I admit I haven't used it much lately, but...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.050
What store is that, anyway?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.990
Cheer up. Keep on trying.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.990
What's she doing with that little kid?

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.810
Sorry to keep you two waiting.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.310
Oujo-sama, how was it?

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.560
Well, as I thought, the price of pots has gone up a bit.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.070
The price of salt is up a little as well.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.070
Prices seem to be rising slowly, so that people hardly notice.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.280
I see.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.440
How could I fail to see it until now?

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.010
Hey...

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.130
What is it, Tan-tan?

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:50.580
What are you guys up to?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:56.340
Housewares, paintings, salt, and that little girl over there just now, how are they all related?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.260
What? They aren't related.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.030
Huh?

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.120
Oh, I thought it was you, Shuurei-dono.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.340
Rin-san!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.930
I heard there's a girl who's been visiting wholesale dealers today, so I came over.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.430
I see.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:16.410
I'd be happy to help, if there's anything I can do.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:20.800
Really? It'd be great if you'd help us!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.440
So, what can I do for you?

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.200
I need you to find out something.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.200
Got it.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.980
Information related to paintings, right?

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.970
Paints, high quality paper, inks, and brushes, I suppose.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:34.710
Yes.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.420
If you could please find out whether one buyer

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.960
has been monopolizing the market for those items, that would help.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.390
Leave it to me.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.180
Oujo-sama, you should rest here with Tan-tan-kun.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.970
Huh? But...

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.730
I'll go see Santa-kun's uncle myself.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.320
I'll be back in no time.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.500
Well, why not?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.360
Excuse me! Could we have two plates of dumplings?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.610
So, I don't understand what you're up to, but are you done?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.770
Sure, we're done for today.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:13.130
"For today"?

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:16.580
There's something that's still bothering me.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.740
We should be done by tomorrow, I think.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.750
Honestly, haven't you done enough?

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.270
Anyway, why not just write a report that says,

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:30.290
"These kinds of fakes seem to be out in the market, can you check it out?"

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.640
Wouldn't that be sufficient?

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.580
You're speaking sense for once.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.340
"For once," is it?

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.440
I'll write a report, of course.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.410
But I'll do it tomorrow, after I find out what's bothering me.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.630
If you're gonna do it, then it's better to do as much as you can.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.680
Originally, I visited the town for...

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.880
You know...

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:58.790
What?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.790
Ouch!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.580
Did you really mean that just now?

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.300
Huh?

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:08.240
That bit about "it's better to do as much as you can."

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.670
It kinda sounded like you were saying that to yourself.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.670
If you really meant it, then I'm impressed.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.960
You were suspended, right?

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.670
If it were me, I'd be shouting, "To hell with all of you!"

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.280
Why do you try so hard?

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.530
In any case, the Imperial Court will run just fine with or without you.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:34.530
If you're there, they'll use you when it's convenient; but if you're not, they won't be concerned.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.760
You're on your own now, right?

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.170
What's in it for you to work so hard?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:44.050
You finally have free time. Why don't you just take it easy?

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.220
I don't understand you.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.630
Tan-tan?

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:48.940
What?

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:55.180
You better hold yourself for a second.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.200
What?

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.030
Ouch!

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.070
What did you do that for?!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.370
Shut up!

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.210
There are times you can't get through unless you pretend to be strong!

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.960
For those I want to impress, I'll pretend I'm strong!

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.710
For those whose approval I need, I won't whine!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:27.090
For those who expect great things of me,
I'll get carried away and meet their expectations!

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.590
Of course I have to be hard on myself!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.590
Ou-Ou-Ou-Ouch!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.370
Even so, there's no way everything in this world will work out!

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:37.890
So there were times I was glad I worked hard!

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:42.640
I'll become a government official like you and save people!

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.520
There were times I was glad I worked hard.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.240
That's why I pretend to be strong.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.240
It's really hard to get back on your feet once you fall down!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.490
What would you do if you couldn't even talk out loud?!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.120
Whether you call it self-satisfaction or a bother,

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:05.250
what else can you do if you don't do what you can?!

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.390
Now that I've vented my anger, I feel like working.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.390
No matter what Tan-tan says,

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.640
I'm just going to work as hard as I want!

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.280
Okay...

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:30.160
Why did I fall for a woman like that?

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.180
Oujo-sama...

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.040
Aren't you having a little too much?

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.400
Oh, Seiran!

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.050
You took your time.

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:47.780
Santa-kun's dad, as we thought.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.670
I see.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:54.800
Tan-tan, when you get home today,
you should secretly check the coins.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.800
There's a good chance your father received counterfeit money as change when he purchased that painting.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.810
Yeah, yeah, got it.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.250
Well then, shall we go home?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.970
Tan-tan, thanks for the food!

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.570
Huh? Hey, wai—

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.570
What?!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.080
I've got to work tonight <i>again?!</i>

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.080
Th-This is bad. I really want to go home as soon as possible!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:38.290
Kochou, I'm thinking of putting this up for display.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:41.360
I've enjoyed it enough by myself.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.350
How about over there?

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.760
You must like this piece a lot, Master.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:55.670
Yes, over there, everyone who comes in can see it.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:59.780
Maybe the creator of this painting will come forward.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.870
Are you okay with that? Fine.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:08.160
Then, why not let Kochou, the fairest blossom of the flower district, hang this painting up for you?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.590
Would you?!

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.170
Thank you so much!

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:21.190
I see. It really is the work of a promising artist.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:21.950
Huh?

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:25.180
This painting... resembles Yukoku's somehow.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.730
I couldn't find it.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:32.480
Karin!

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:35.310
What are you looking for?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.330
Kochou, just one question first .

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:42.860
Did a dull-looking oaf come looking for me?

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.830
Not that I know of.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.570
Such a hopeless oaf!

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:52.010
Huh?

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.340
What's that painting?

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.710
Oh, you noticed it too?

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.060
It's quite a piece—

00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.840
I found it!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.220
The tree specialist and the gardener!

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.900
Karin! Hey!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.370
Someone!

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.860
"The tree specialist and the gardener"?

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.130
It's... It's gone!

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.190
When I woke up, Karin was already gone and...

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:59.280
I'll definitely bring the painting back later.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.220
I'm just borrowing it for a little while.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.500
That's what her note said.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:13.080
Tan-tan! You came all the way here?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:19.090
Your scary retainer said I'd be cursed by the raccoon if I didn't.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:19.980
What?

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:26.740
Anyway, it's only for today, even for me.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:27.910
Thanks a lot.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:29.460
Well, shall we go?

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.100
Where?

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:34.950
I don't know if I can meet him, but let's try anyway.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.820
Come, please take a look.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.240
Here, what do you think?

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.640
Have a good look at it.

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:55.720
What's wrong, Shuei?

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.250
Have you lost Karin?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.200
No.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:03.260
Yesterday, she was running around the town making an awful fuss, but...

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.320
But what?

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:07.260
Which art dealer is it this time?

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.750
No, it's not an art dealer this time.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:14.580
She seems to be accosting every gardener and tree specialist in Kiyou.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:15.890
What?!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.100
That was perfect timing!

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:20.400
I just got back too.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.700
You work even on a public holiday?

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:26.340
Rather, we've been extremely busy of late.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.320
I've been staying at the palace all this time.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:31.030
I haven't taken a bath in three days.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.040
Wh-What's up with all of you?!

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:47.360
Seriously, how can she work so hard?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:54.680
Look at me. I hate hard work, and I give up quickly.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.500
I don't even think of changing the world.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.880
It won't change much anyway.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:00.970
Won't it?

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.570
No, it won't.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.940
For instance, that girl yesterday...

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:06.630
What?

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:09.990
Oh, that girl who was crying in front of the housewares store.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:14.040
Yes, that girl's mother... passed away recently.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.000
She never recovered from childbirth.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.230
What?

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:20.720
At the time, her father was away peddling,

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.660
and she didn't know what to do with her newborn brother.

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:28.390
So she came to oujo-sama's house.

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:29.590
Oh...

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:34.050
So oujo-sama quickly contacted the mothers in the girl's neighborhood

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:36.450
and helped settle the matter.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:40.500
So yesterday, she came to thank oujo-sama, as well as to ask for a favor.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.130
She said, "Please reduce the number of women dying like my mother."

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.360
I don't call that giving thanks!

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.860
What are government officials supposed to be, sob sisters?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:53.870
But, who can you talk to if you can't talk to a government official?

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:59.790
Last night, oujo-sama must've written a report on the forgeries as well as about fatalities in childbirth.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.300
No way...

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.990
She didn't come visit the town just because of the forgeries.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:08.330
Ever since she returned from Sashuu,

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:11.380
she's visited the town every day,
seeing and asking about various issues.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.010
Every day?!

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:16.540
It was only by coincidence that we ran into this counterfeiting case yesterday.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.570
I don't believe this.

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:20.770
I can't do it, no way.

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.440
They're all fakes.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:27.860
I thought so.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.320
There's no mistake.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.860
I pride myself on being the best connoisseur in the Heki family,

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.520
although I have no artistic talent myself.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:37.120
But... why did you bring all of them to me?

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:42.320
I think I've seen this one somewhere, probably the original.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:43.960
Oh...

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:50.420
That was on special display at the Palace Court party for the candidates who passed the National Examination.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.510
As expected of Hakumei-kun! I thought you might remember.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:57.880
If I recall correctly, it was painted for that year's successful candidates.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:01.320
After the party, it should've been stored at the Arts Department.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:03.710
Yes, that's what I heard too.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.900
Which makes this odd...

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:09.310
Whoever can forge this painting must be...

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.900
You'd...

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:14.120
better stay out of this from now on.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:14.610
What?

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.440
If a government official is behind this,

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:20.620
then the Government Inspectorate is probably involved already.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.160
The Government Inspectorate...

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.860
They investigate official corruption

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.340
and can even take measures against officials independently.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:30.890
If you continue to involve yourself, you'll be exceeding your authority.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:35.890
I've heard that the current Secretary of the Government Inspectorate is conceited and unforgiving.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:40.140
In any case, I'll keep this counterfeit money and the forgeries.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:44.300
The forged money especially could cause you big trouble.

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:55.720
Brother!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.330
I thought you might be here, brother!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.590
Where's sister?

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:03.000
Well, you see, Hakumei-kun...

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:07.000
I didn't want to worry you more, if at all possible.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.750
Brother, I'm happy to hear that you worry about me, but...

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:14.140
These are...

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:19.050
Brother, you know who painted these, don't you?

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.220
Yeah.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:23.730
Why create forgeries like these?

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.350
Where is Karin-nee-san?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.380
I only arrived in Kiyou recently,

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:32.890
but I've been looking for Karin for two months.

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:35.360
So I guess you don't know where she is either.

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.000
Rather than looking for my sister,

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.210
you'd do better to stop the production of these forgeries.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.370
Yes, I think so too.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.790
Seriously, we've got to do something about it,
as members of the Heki family!

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.380
Oh, she was here all right.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.820
A weird but beautiful woman, just now.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:57.030
She showed me this painting,

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:00.260
and asked me if I knew where the garden in the painting could be found.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.880
And... what did you say?

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.680
I said, "Sure I do."

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.770
She asked me where and then dashed off.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.270
You know the place?

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.820
Of course! I created that garden with great pain and care!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.240
If anyone knows it, I would.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.280
Where is it?! Please tell us!

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.670
It's blooming.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:37.930
Huh? Why are you in the garden?

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:40.930
Tan-tan! What are you doing here?

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:44.590
Well, don't you have a guard at the entrance?

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:47.500
So if I had any business, I'd have to come in without permission.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.940
Conveniently, the wall over there has broken down, so I came in that way.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:53.390
Anyway, why don't you fix it? It's dangerous.

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:55.960
Ah, thanks for your concern.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.520
Wait, that's not the point.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:00.020
What's your business with me?

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:06.330
Well, no matter how I look at you, you're really not my type of girl.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:09.050
You came here to pick a fight with me?

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:14.320
So, I decided I wouldn't listen to what my dad told me this time.

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:18.970
You try way too hard, and you're really too good.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.340
You just get on my nerves.

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:25.350
Staying with you feels exhausting.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:31.210
You must truly believe in your sense of justice and all sorts of other nice stuff too.

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:35.360
I thought, how sickening is that?

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.360
I don't know if...

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:44.460
what you say is true, but I don't think society will go easy on you.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:50.370
Then again, you never said "Why don't you try harder?" to me, did you?

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:53.090
D-Didn't I?

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:54.380
No.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.730
That's the only thing that gave me pause.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:02.980
If you'd said that, even just once, I suppose even a calm guy like me would've been annoyed.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:04.400
Is that so?

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:08.630
But you didn't, so I'll show you my gratitude for that.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:10.640
Huh? Show your gratitude?

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:16.400
I remember just one thing that my mother told me.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.040
She said something like,

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:23.650
"You can live whatever life you like, but stay out of the way of people who are trying really hard."

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:26.870
I don't see where this conversation is going.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.660
She was useless as a mother.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.610
Come with me, and you'll know what I mean.

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:37.250
But if I take just you, I think your scary family retainer will scold me, so bring him along as well.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:40.250
Huh? What?

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.520
Stop! Stop!

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:10.470
What's wrong with this wall!

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:12.410
How dare it obstruct me!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:13.700
It's exceedingly insulting!

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:15.790
I will never forgive this!

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.390
Here, take this, this and that!

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:18.710
There! Again!

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:25.550
Well, Kouyu's prophecy came true.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:26.990
Seriously!

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:28.520
E-Excuse me...

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.770
Karin-san?

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:31.590
What?!

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:32.320
No!

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:33.630
What's going on?!

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:36.800
What are these dowdy men doing here?! Three of them!

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.110
I can't stand this! Shoo! Get lost!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:44.490
Th-This is what Kochou meant by "a little harsh on men."

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.730
Kochou?

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:47.940
You mean Kochou at Kougarou?

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:49.860
Yes.

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:52.890
Kochou told us about you, and we've been out looking for you.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.500
Why me?

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.170
We want to know where Heki Yukoku is.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.000
We'd like you to tell us anything about him.

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:21.640
Why... are you here?

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.780
What's this gathering about?

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:29.780
If you've got business with our family, the entrance gate is over there.

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:33.100
What? This is your home?

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.410
Yeah.

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:55.060
What you're seeking is right in here.

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:04.070
Banri!

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:10.090
Mother...

00:23:10.090 --> 00:23:11.160
Mother!

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:14.660
Mother!

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:16.770
Mother...

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:18.020
Banri...

00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:22.880
Mother...

00:24:45.550 --> 00:24:47.960
We finally found Karin-san.

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:49.840
But what's Ryuuki doing here?

00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:52.210
Whose residence is this?

00:24:52.210 --> 00:24:54.790
What? It's Tan-tan's home?!

00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:56.260
What's going on here?!
